// `and` and `or` stop as soon as the result is known: the right side is not
// evaluated, so it has no side effect. The counter of `probe` shows which sides
// were evaluated, in when conditions, if statements, choice option conditions
// and interpolations.

state
  count: 0
  gold: 20

function probe(value)
  count = count + 1
  return value

beat Start
  // Plain conditions
  if false and probe(true)
    Not here.
  if true or probe(true)
    Skipped the right side.
  Probed $count times.

  count = 0
  if true and probe(true)
    Both sides.
  if false or probe(true)
    Both sides again.
  Probed $count times.

  // A chain stops at the first false clause
  count = 0
  if probe(true) and probe(false) and probe(true) and probe(true)
    Not here.
  Probed $count times.

  // When conditions: every rule is evaluated, each one short-circuits
  count = 0
  when
    gold > 100 and probe(true)
      Rich.
    gold > 10 and probe(true)
      Comfortable.
    true
      Broke.
  Probed $count times.

  // Choice option conditions
  count = 0
  choice
    Buy if gold > 100 and probe(true)
      Bought.
    Look if gold > 10 or probe(true)
      Looked.
  Probed $count times.

  // Interpolations
  count = 0
  The result is ${false and probe(true)}, ${true or probe(true)} and ${gold > 10 and probe(true)}.
  Probed $count times.

/*
<test>
- choices: [1]
  expected: |
    ~ Skipped the right side.

    ~ Probed 0 times.

    ~ Both sides.

    ~ Both sides again.

    ~ Probed 2 times.

    ~ Probed 2 times.

    ~ Comfortable.

    ~ Probed 1 times.

    - Buy
    + Look

    ~ Looked.

    ~ Probed 0 times.

    ~ The result is false, true and true.
      Probed 1 times.
</test>
*/
